      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Where Terraform Fits\nTerraform can manage any product that has an\nAPI and a provider. The [Terraform\nRegistry](https://registry.terraform.io/)\npublishes the providers. On 2026-11-16, the\nRegistry listed these providers for the\nproducts in this stack:\n\n| Product | Provider | Latest version |\nExample resource types |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Snowflake | [`snowflakedb/snowflake`](https:\n//registry.terraform.io/providers/snowflakedb/\nsnowflake/latest/docs) | 2.23.0 |\n`snowflake_database`, `snowflake_schema`,\n`snowflake_warehouse`,\n`snowflake_account_role`,\n`snowflake_grant_privileges_to_account_role`,\n`snowflake_external_volume` |\n| Aiven for Apache Kafka | [`aiven/aiven`](htt\nps://registry.terraform.io/providers/aiven/aiv\nen/latest/docs) | 4.66.0 | `aiven_kafka`,\n`aiven_kafka_topic`, `aiven_kafka_user`,\n`aiven_kafka_acl`, `aiven_kafka_connector` |\n| dbt Cloud | [`dbt-labs/dbtcloud`](https://re\ngistry.terraform.io/providers/dbt-labs/dbtclou\nd/latest/docs) | 1.12.13 | `dbtcloud_project`,\n`dbtcloud_environment`, `dbtcloud_job` |\n| AWS, for the S3 bucket of Iceberg files | [`\nhashicorp/aws`](https://registry.terraform.io/\nproviders/hashicorp/aws/latest/docs) | 6.73.0\n| `aws_s3_bucket`, `aws_iam_role` |\n\nSnowflake says that its provider manages\n\"warehouses, databases, schemas, tables,\nroles, grants, and more\" ([Snowflake Terraform\nprovider](https://docs.snowflake.com/en/user-g\nuide/terraform)).\n\nEach object needs one owner. Terraform changes\nonly the objects in its configuration and\nstate. Other tools create other objects:\n\n- dbt creates the tables and views of its\nmodels each time it runs. No Terraform state\nlists them. The [dbt\nmap](../dbt/dbt-deep-mental-model.md)\ndescribes dbt.\n- A Kafka producer writes events into a topic.\nTerraform can create the topic and its ACLs.\nThe events are data, not infrastructure. The\n[Kafka map](../kafka/kafka.md) describes\nKafka.\n- An Iceberg sink writes Parquet and metadata\nfiles into a bucket. Terraform can create the\nbucket and the roles that may write to it. The\n[Iceberg map](../iceberg/iceberg.md) describes\nIceberg.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-45d19e1c479c",
      "originalText": "Where Terraform Fits\nTerraform can manage any product that has an API and a provider. The [Terraform Registry](https://registry.terraform.io/) publishes the providers. On 2026-11-16, the Registry listed these providers for the products in this stack:\n\n| Product | Provider | Latest version | Example resource types |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Snowflake | [`snowflakedb/snowflake`](https://registry.terraform.io/providers/snowflakedb/snowflake/latest/docs) | 2.23.0 | `snowflake_database`, `snowflake_schema`, `snowflake_warehouse`, `snowflake_account_role`, `snowflake_grant_privileges_to_account_role`, `snowflake_external_volume` |\n| Aiven for Apache Kafka | [`aiven/aiven`](https://registry.terraform.io/providers/aiven/aiven/latest/docs) | 4.66.0 | `aiven_kafka`, `aiven_kafka_topic`, `aiven_kafka_user`, `aiven_kafka_acl`, `aiven_kafka_connector` |\n| dbt Cloud | [`dbt-labs/dbtcloud`](https://registry.terraform.io/providers/dbt-labs/dbtcloud/latest/docs) | 1.12.13 | `dbtcloud_project`, `dbtcloud_environment`, `dbtcloud_job` |\n| AWS, for the S3 bucket of Iceberg files | [`hashicorp/aws`](https://registry.terraform.io/providers/hashicorp/aws/latest/docs) | 6.73.0 | `aws_s3_bucket`, `aws_iam_role` |\n\nSnowflake says that its provider manages \"warehouses, databases, schemas, tables, roles, grants, and more\" ([Snowflake Terraform provider](https://docs.snowflake.com/en/user-guide/terraform)).\n\nEach object needs one owner. Terraform changes only the objects in its configuration and state. Other tools create other objects:\n\n- dbt creates the tables and views of its models each time it runs. No Terraform state lists them. The [dbt map](../dbt/dbt-deep-mental-model.md) describes dbt.\n- A Kafka producer writes events into a topic. Terraform can create the topic and its ACLs. The events are data, not infrastructure. The [Kafka map](../kafka/kafka.md) describes Kafka.\n- An Iceberg sink writes Parquet and metadata files into a bucket. Terraform can create the bucket and the roles that may write to it. The [Iceberg map](../iceberg/iceberg.md) describes Iceberg.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "where-terraform-fits"
      }
    },
