      "locked": false,
      "text": "Configuration and HCL\nTerraform code is called configuration. You\nwrite it in HCL, the HashiCorp Configuration\nLanguage, in files with the extension `.tf` ([\nsyntax](https://developer.hashicorp.com/terraf\norm/language/syntax/configuration)). A\nconfiguration is a list of blocks. A block has\na type, zero or more labels, and a body of\narguments in braces:\n\n```hcl\nresource \"snowflake_warehouse\" \"transform\" {\nname           =\n\"TRANSFORM_${local.suffix}_WH\"\nwarehouse_size = \"XSMALL\"\nauto_suspend   = 60\n}\n```\n\nHere `resource` is the block type.\n`snowflake_warehouse` is the resource type,\nwhich the Snowflake provider defines.\n`transform` is a local name that only\nTerraform uses. `name`, `warehouse_size` and\n`auto_suspend` are arguments. `${...}` inserts\nthe value of an expression into a string.\n\nA configuration uses these block types:\n\n- `terraform`: the Terraform version, the\nproviders and their versions, and the backend.\n- `provider`: the connection settings of one\nprovider.\n- `resource`: an object that Terraform\ncreates, changes and deletes.\n- `data`: an object that Terraform only reads.\n- `variable`: an input value.\n- `locals`: named expressions inside one\nmodule.\n- `output`: a value that the module returns.\n- `module`: a call to another module.\n- `moved` and `import`: instructions that\nchange what the state records.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-5121d75a8dac",
      "originalText": "Configuration and HCL\nTerraform code is called configuration. You write it in HCL, the HashiCorp Configuration Language, in files with the extension `.tf` ([syntax](https://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/syntax/configuration)). A configuration is a list of blocks. A block has a type, zero or more labels, and a body of arguments in braces:\n\n```hcl\nresource \"snowflake_warehouse\" \"transform\" {\n  name           = \"TRANSFORM_${local.suffix}_WH\"\n  warehouse_size = \"XSMALL\"\n  auto_suspend   = 60\n}\n```\n\nHere `resource` is the block type. `snowflake_warehouse` is the resource type, which the Snowflake provider defines. `transform` is a local name that only Terraform uses. `name`, `warehouse_size` and `auto_suspend` are arguments. `${...}` inserts the value of an expression into a string.\n\nA configuration uses these block types:\n\n- `terraform`: the Terraform version, the providers and their versions, and the backend.\n- `provider`: the connection settings of one provider.\n- `resource`: an object that Terraform creates, changes and deletes.\n- `data`: an object that Terraform only reads.\n- `variable`: an input value.\n- `locals`: named expressions inside one module.\n- `output`: a value that the module returns.\n- `module`: a call to another module.\n- `moved` and `import`: instructions that change what the state records.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "configuration-and-hcl"
      }
    },
