      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Resource\nA resource block declares one object that\nTerraform creates, changes and deletes. The\nresource type comes from a provider. This\ntopic comes from the Aiven provider's example \n([`aiven_kafka_topic`](https://registry.terraf\norm.io/providers/aiven/aiven/latest/docs/resou\nrces/kafka_topic)):\n\n```hcl\nresource \"aiven_kafka_topic\" \"orders\" {\nproject      = \"my-project\"\nservice_name = \"my-kafka\"\ntopic_name   = \"orders\"\npartitions   = 3\nreplication  = 3\n}\n```\n\nTerraform names each object by its address:\nthe resource type, a dot, and the local name,\nhere `aiven_kafka_topic.orders`. In a child\nmodule, the address starts with the module\npath, as in\n`module.kafka.aiven_kafka_topic.orders`. A\nblock with `for_each` makes one object for\neach key, as in\n`aiven_kafka_topic.cdc[\"orders\"]` ([resource a\nddressing](https://developer.hashicorp.com/ter\nraform/cli/state/resource-addressing)). Plan\noutput, the state, and `moved` and `import`\nblocks all use addresses.\n\nAnother block reads an attribute through the\naddress, for example\n`aiven_kafka_topic.orders.topic_name`.\nTerraform infers from such a reference that\nthe topic must exist first. The `depends_on`\nargument is only for a dependency that no\nreference shows ([depends_on](https://develope\nr.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/meta-argume\nnts/depends_on)).",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-7a1047389735",
      "originalText": "Resource\nA resource block declares one object that Terraform creates, changes and deletes. The resource type comes from a provider. This topic comes from the Aiven provider's example ([`aiven_kafka_topic`](https://registry.terraform.io/providers/aiven/aiven/latest/docs/resources/kafka_topic)):\n\n```hcl\nresource \"aiven_kafka_topic\" \"orders\" {\n  project      = \"my-project\"\n  service_name = \"my-kafka\"\n  topic_name   = \"orders\"\n  partitions   = 3\n  replication  = 3\n}\n```\n\nTerraform names each object by its address: the resource type, a dot, and the local name, here `aiven_kafka_topic.orders`. In a child module, the address starts with the module path, as in `module.kafka.aiven_kafka_topic.orders`. A block with `for_each` makes one object for each key, as in `aiven_kafka_topic.cdc[\"orders\"]` ([resource addressing](https://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/cli/state/resource-addressing)). Plan output, the state, and `moved` and `import` blocks all use addresses.\n\nAnother block reads an attribute through the address, for example `aiven_kafka_topic.orders.topic_name`. Terraform infers from such a reference that the topic must exist first. The `depends_on` argument is only for a dependency that no reference shows ([depends_on](https://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/meta-arguments/depends_on)).",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "resource"
      }
    },
