      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Module\nA module is the set of `.tf` files in one\nfolder. Terraform does not read subfolders:\neach subfolder is a separate module ([files\nand directories](https://developer.hashicorp.c\nom/terraform/language/files)). The root module\nis the folder where you run Terraform. A child\nmodule is a module that another module calls\nwith a `module` block:\n\n```hcl\nmodule \"orders_topic\" {\nsource     = \"./modules/kafka-topic\"\ntopic_name = \"orders\"\npartitions = 3\n}\n```\n\n`source` says where the module is. It can be a\nlocal path, which must begin with `./` or\n`../`, a Terraform Registry address with a\n`version`, or a Git URL ([module sources](http\ns://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/language\n/modules/sources)). The other arguments fill\nthe variables of the child module. The\naddresses of the child's resources start with\n`module.orders_topic.`.\n\nA module works like a function. Its variables\nare the parameters, its resources are the\nbody, and its outputs are the return values.\nThe root module and all the modules that it\ncalls form one configuration, and all their\nobjects go into one state.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-fbd34a2b6e6a",
      "originalText": "Module\nA module is the set of `.tf` files in one folder. Terraform does not read subfolders: each subfolder is a separate module ([files and directories](https://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/files)). The root module is the folder where you run Terraform. A child module is a module that another module calls with a `module` block:\n\n```hcl\nmodule \"orders_topic\" {\n  source     = \"./modules/kafka-topic\"\n  topic_name = \"orders\"\n  partitions = 3\n}\n```\n\n`source` says where the module is. It can be a local path, which must begin with `./` or `../`, a Terraform Registry address with a `version`, or a Git URL ([module sources](https://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/modules/sources)). The other arguments fill the variables of the child module. The addresses of the child's resources start with `module.orders_topic.`.\n\nA module works like a function. Its variables are the parameters, its resources are the body, and its outputs are the return values. The root module and all the modules that it calls form one configuration, and all their objects go into one state.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "module"
      }
    },
