      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "State\nState is Terraform's record of the objects\nthat it manages. Its main job is to bind each\nresource address to one real object ([purpose\nof state](https://developer.hashicorp.com/terr\naform/language/state/purpose)). Without the\nstate, Terraform cannot tell whether a\nwarehouse in Snowflake belongs to\n`snowflake_warehouse.transform` or to someone\nelse.\n\nBy default, the state is the file\n`terraform.tfstate` in the root module folder.\nTerraform keeps the previous version in\n`terraform.tfstate.backup` ([state](https://de\nveloper.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/state\n)). The file is JSON. This excerpt comes from\nthe import in About the Examples. The real\nfile has 4,445 bytes, and the warehouse has 23\nattributes. The excerpt leaves out most\nattributes and some other fields:\n\n```json\n{\n\"version\": 4,\n\"terraform_version\": \"1.15.8\",\n\"resources\": [\n{\n\"mode\": \"managed\",\n\"type\": \"snowflake_warehouse\",\n\"name\": \"agent\",\n\"provider\": \"provider[\\\"registry.terraform.io/\nsnowflakedb/snowflake\\\"]\",\n\"instances\": [\n{\n\"attributes\": {\n\"auto_resume\": \"true\",\n\"auto_suspend\": 60,\n\"id\": \"\\\"AGENT_WH\\\"\",\n\"name\": \"AGENT_WH\",\n\"warehouse_size\": \"XSMALL\"\n}\n}\n]\n}\n]\n}\n```\n\n`type` and `name` together give the address\n`snowflake_warehouse.agent`. `id` is the key\nwith which the provider finds the object\nagain. For a Snowflake warehouse, the ID is\nthe name in double quotes. Do not edit the\nfile by hand. The commands `terraform state\nlist`, `terraform state show`, `terraform\nstate mv` and `terraform state rm` read and\nchange it ([state commands](https://developer.\nhashicorp.com/terraform/cli/state)).",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-aa4a5f8125f2",
      "originalText": "State\nState is Terraform's record of the objects that it manages. Its main job is to bind each resource address to one real object ([purpose of state](https://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/state/purpose)). Without the state, Terraform cannot tell whether a warehouse in Snowflake belongs to `snowflake_warehouse.transform` or to someone else.\n\nBy default, the state is the file `terraform.tfstate` in the root module folder. Terraform keeps the previous version in `terraform.tfstate.backup` ([state](https://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/state)). The file is JSON. This excerpt comes from the import in About the Examples. The real file has 4,445 bytes, and the warehouse has 23 attributes. The excerpt leaves out most attributes and some other fields:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"version\": 4,\n  \"terraform_version\": \"1.15.8\",\n  \"resources\": [\n    {\n      \"mode\": \"managed\",\n      \"type\": \"snowflake_warehouse\",\n      \"name\": \"agent\",\n      \"provider\": \"provider[\\\"registry.terraform.io/snowflakedb/snowflake\\\"]\",\n      \"instances\": [\n        {\n          \"attributes\": {\n            \"auto_resume\": \"true\",\n            \"auto_suspend\": 60,\n            \"id\": \"\\\"AGENT_WH\\\"\",\n            \"name\": \"AGENT_WH\",\n            \"warehouse_size\": \"XSMALL\"\n          }\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n`type` and `name` together give the address `snowflake_warehouse.agent`. `id` is the key with which the provider finds the object again. For a Snowflake warehouse, the ID is the name in double quotes. Do not edit the file by hand. The commands `terraform state list`, `terraform state show`, `terraform state mv` and `terraform state rm` read and change it ([state commands](https://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/cli/state)).",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "state"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "rectangle",
      "version": 1,
