    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 8037722996,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "text-62fdfbd55d19",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 1919.2,
      "y": 2200.0,
      "strokeColor": "#1E3A8A",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 394.8,
      "height": 507.5,
      "seed": 218371,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Import\nImport brings an object that already exists\nunder Terraform management. Terraform reads\nthe object and writes it into the state.\nImport does not change the object ([import](ht\ntps://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/langua\nge/import)). A team uses import to adopt\nobjects that someone created by hand.\n\nThe command form writes the state at once. In\nAbout the Examples, this command read an\nexisting warehouse with a read-only role:\n\n`terraform import snowflake_warehouse.agent\n'\"AGENT_WH\"'`\n\nEach provider's docs give the ID format. For a\nSnowflake warehouse, it is the name in double\nquotes ([warehouse import](https://registry.te\nrraform.io/providers/snowflakedb/snowflake/lat\nest/docs/resources/warehouse#import)). An\n`import` block in a `.tf` file does the same\njob through a normal plan and apply, so a\nreviewer sees the import in the plan first\n([import block](https://developer.hashicorp.co\nm/terraform/language/block/import)). After an\nimport, read the next plan line by line.\nOutside Changes Get Reverted shows the first\nplan after this import.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-62fdfbd55d19",
      "originalText": "Import\nImport brings an object that already exists under Terraform management. Terraform reads the object and writes it into the state. Import does not change the object ([import](https://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/import)). A team uses import to adopt objects that someone created by hand.\n\nThe command form writes the state at once. In About the Examples, this command read an existing warehouse with a read-only role:\n\n`terraform import snowflake_warehouse.agent '\"AGENT_WH\"'`\n\nEach provider's docs give the ID format. For a Snowflake warehouse, it is the name in double quotes ([warehouse import](https://registry.terraform.io/providers/snowflakedb/snowflake/latest/docs/resources/warehouse#import)). An `import` block in a `.tf` file does the same job through a normal plan and apply, so a reviewer sees the import in the plan first ([import block](https://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/block/import)). After an import, read the next plan line by line. Outside Changes Get Reverted shows the first plan after this import.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "import"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "rectangle",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 9413954540,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "node-2d8b0709a4fd",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 1907.2,
      "y": 2460.0,
      "strokeColor": "#1E3A8A",
      "backgroundColor": "#F8FAFC",
      "width": 418.8,
      "height": 220,
      "seed": 643393,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
