    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 5881211691,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "text-a279fe916f63",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 1310.4,
      "y": 2980.0,
      "strokeColor": "#1E3A8A",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 394.8,
      "height": 525.0,
      "seed": 192668,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Workspace\nA CLI workspace is one more state for the same\nconfiguration and the same backend ([workspace\ns](https://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/l\nanguage/state/workspaces)). Every backend\nstarts with the workspace `default`. The\ncommands `terraform workspace new prod` and\n`terraform workspace select prod` choose the\nstate that the next plan uses. Code reads the\ncurrent name as `terraform.workspace`:\n\n```hcl\nresource \"snowflake_warehouse\" \"transform\" {\nname           =\n\"TRANSFORM_${upper(terraform.workspace)}_WH\"\nwarehouse_size = terraform.workspace == \"prod\"\n? \"LARGE\" : \"XSMALL\"\n}\n```\n\nWith the S3 backend, the state of the\nworkspace `prod` lives at `env:/prod/<key>` in\nthe bucket ([S3 backend](https://developer.has\nhicorp.com/terraform/language/backend/s3)).\nHashiCorp advises against CLI workspaces for\nenvironments that need separate credentials\nand access controls ([CLI workspaces](https://\ndeveloper.hashicorp.com/terraform/cli/workspac\nes)). HCP Terraform also uses the word\nworkspace, for a different object.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-a279fe916f63",
      "originalText": "Workspace\nA CLI workspace is one more state for the same configuration and the same backend ([workspaces](https://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/state/workspaces)). Every backend starts with the workspace `default`. The commands `terraform workspace new prod` and `terraform workspace select prod` choose the state that the next plan uses. Code reads the current name as `terraform.workspace`:\n\n```hcl\nresource \"snowflake_warehouse\" \"transform\" {\n  name           = \"TRANSFORM_${upper(terraform.workspace)}_WH\"\n  warehouse_size = terraform.workspace == \"prod\" ? \"LARGE\" : \"XSMALL\"\n}\n```\n\nWith the S3 backend, the state of the workspace `prod` lives at `env:/prod/<key>` in the bucket ([S3 backend](https://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/backend/s3)). HashiCorp advises against CLI workspaces for environments that need separate credentials and access controls ([CLI workspaces](https://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/cli/workspaces)). HCP Terraform also uses the word workspace, for a different object.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "workspace"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "rectangle",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 8312755764,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "node-bed97175b06e",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 1298.4,
      "y": 3370.0,
      "strokeColor": "#1E3A8A",
      "backgroundColor": "#F8FAFC",
