      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Replacement Destroys Data\nSome arguments cannot change on a live object.\nA change to such an argument makes a replace\n(`-/+`), and the plan marks the argument with\n`# forces replacement`. For an\n`aiven_kafka_topic`, a change to `topic_name`,\n`project` or `service_name` forces a new topic\n([Aiven topic docs](https://registry.terraform\n.io/providers/aiven/aiven/latest/docs/resource\ns/kafka_topic)). A new topic name in the\nconfiguration therefore deletes the topic with\nall its messages, and creates an empty topic.\n\n`lifecycle { prevent_destroy = true }` in a\nresource block makes Terraform reject every\nplan that destroys the object. It does not\nprotect the object when someone deletes the\nwhole block, because Terraform then no longer\nreads the setting ([lifecycle](https://develop\ner.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/meta-argum\nents/lifecycle)).",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-a171b546f733",
      "originalText": "Replacement Destroys Data\nSome arguments cannot change on a live object. A change to such an argument makes a replace (`-/+`), and the plan marks the argument with `# forces replacement`. For an `aiven_kafka_topic`, a change to `topic_name`, `project` or `service_name` forces a new topic ([Aiven topic docs](https://registry.terraform.io/providers/aiven/aiven/latest/docs/resources/kafka_topic)). A new topic name in the configuration therefore deletes the topic with all its messages, and creates an empty topic.\n\n`lifecycle { prevent_destroy = true }` in a resource block makes Terraform reject every plan that destroys the object. It does not protect the object when someone deletes the whole block, because Terraform then no longer reads the setting ([lifecycle](https://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/meta-arguments/lifecycle)).",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "replacement-destroys-data"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "rectangle",
