    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 2187893231,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "text-9640580c8c78",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 1332.0,
      "y": 3760.0,
      "strokeColor": "#1E3A8A",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 394.8,
      "height": 1277.5,
      "seed": 772086,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "File Names\nTerraform reads every `.tf` and `.tf.json`\nfile in a folder as one document. The split\ninto files has no effect on what Terraform\ndoes ([files and directories](https://develope\nr.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/files)). So\na resource in `main.tf` works the same in\n`warehouses.tf`. Only these names have a\nmeaning for Terraform:\n\n| Name | What Terraform does with it | In Git\n|\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `*.tf`, `*.tf.json` | Reads all of them in\nthe folder as configuration. | Yes |\n| `override.tf`, `*_override.tf` | Reads them\nlast, and merges each block into the block of\nthe same name ([override files](https://develo\nper.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/files/ove\nrride)). | Yes |\n| `terraform.tfvars`, `terraform.tfvars.json`\n| Loads the variable values automatically. |\nYes, without secrets |\n| `*.auto.tfvars`, `*.auto.tfvars.json` |\nLoads the variable values automatically, in\nlexical order. | Yes, without secrets |\n| Any other `*.tfvars` | Loads the values only\nwith `-var-file=<file>`. | Yes, without\nsecrets |\n| `.terraform.lock.hcl` | Records the provider\nversions and checksums that `init` chose\n([lock file](https://developer.hashicorp.com/t\nerraform/language/files/dependency-lock)). |\nYes |\n| `.terraform/` | Holds the downloaded\nproviders and modules. | No |\n| `terraform.tfstate`,\n`terraform.tfstate.backup` | Local state. | No\n|\n| `.terraform.tfstate.lock.info` | Local state\nlock. | No |\n| The file after `plan -out=` | Saved plan. |\nNo |\n| `*.tftest.hcl` | Tests for `terraform test`\n([test files](https://developer.hashicorp.com/\nterraform/language/files/tests)). | Yes |\n\nThe \"In Git\" column follows the [style guide](\nhttps://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/lang\nuage/style#gitignore).\n\nOther names are a convention for readers. The\nstyle guide recommends these names ([file name\ns](https://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/l\nanguage/style#file-names)):\n\n- `terraform.tf`: the `terraform` block with\n`required_version` and `required_providers`.\nThe public [S3 bucket module](https://github.c\nom/terraform-aws-modules/terraform-aws-s3-buck\net) names this file `versions.tf`.\n- `backend.tf`: the backend configuration.\n- `providers.tf`: the `provider` blocks.\n- `variables.tf`, `outputs.tf`, `locals.tf`:\nthe `variable`, `output` and `locals` blocks.\n- `main.tf`: the resource and data blocks.\n\nA configuration can split `main.tf` by\nsubject, for example into `warehouses.tf`,\n`topics.tf` or `grants.tf`. Files such as\n`moved.tf` or `imports.tf` collect `moved` and\n`import` blocks. Terraform treats all of them\nas ordinary `.tf` files.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-9640580c8c78",
      "originalText": "File Names\nTerraform reads every `.tf` and `.tf.json` file in a folder as one document. The split into files has no effect on what Terraform does ([files and directories](https://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/files)). So a resource in `main.tf` works the same in `warehouses.tf`. Only these names have a meaning for Terraform:\n\n| Name | What Terraform does with it | In Git |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `*.tf`, `*.tf.json` | Reads all of them in the folder as configuration. | Yes |\n| `override.tf`, `*_override.tf` | Reads them last, and merges each block into the block of the same name ([override files](https://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/files/override)). | Yes |\n| `terraform.tfvars`, `terraform.tfvars.json` | Loads the variable values automatically. | Yes, without secrets |\n| `*.auto.tfvars`, `*.auto.tfvars.json` | Loads the variable values automatically, in lexical order. | Yes, without secrets |\n| Any other `*.tfvars` | Loads the values only with `-var-file=<file>`. | Yes, without secrets |\n| `.terraform.lock.hcl` | Records the provider versions and checksums that `init` chose ([lock file](https://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/files/dependency-lock)). | Yes |\n| `.terraform/` | Holds the downloaded providers and modules. | No |\n| `terraform.tfstate`, `terraform.tfstate.backup` | Local state. | No |\n| `.terraform.tfstate.lock.info` | Local state lock. | No |\n| The file after `plan -out=` | Saved plan. | No |\n| `*.tftest.hcl` | Tests for `terraform test` ([test files](https://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/files/tests)). | Yes |\n\nThe \"In Git\" column follows the [style guide](https://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/style#gitignore).\n\nOther names are a convention for readers. The style guide recommends these names ([file names](https://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/style#file-names)):\n\n- `terraform.tf`: the `terraform` block with `required_version` and `required_providers`. The public [S3 bucket module](https://github.com/terraform-aws-modules/terraform-aws-s3-bucket) names this file `versions.tf`.\n- `backend.tf`: the backend configuration.\n- `providers.tf`: the `provider` blocks.\n- `variables.tf`, `outputs.tf`, `locals.tf`: the `variable`, `output` and `locals` blocks.\n- `main.tf`: the resource and data blocks.\n\nA configuration can split `main.tf` by subject, for example into `warehouses.tf`, `topics.tf` or `grants.tf`. Files such as `moved.tf` or `imports.tf` collect `moved` and `import` blocks. Terraform treats all of them as ordinary `.tf` files.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "file-names"
      }
    },
