      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Repo Layouts\nThe style guide shows three ways to separate\nenvironments and parts of the system\n([multiple environments](https://developer.has\nhicorp.com/terraform/language/style#multiple-e\nnvironments)):\n\n- One folder for each environment, such as\n`dev/`, `staging/` and `prod/`. Each folder\nhas its own `backend.tf`, so each environment\nhas its own state. All of them call the shared\nmodules in `modules/`.\n- One folder for each part of the system, such\nas `networking/`, `database/` and `compute/`.\nEach part has its own state, so a change in\none part cannot touch the objects of another\npart.\n- One configuration with one workspace for\neach environment. The Workspace node describes\nthe limits of CLI workspaces.\n\nValues that differ by environment can sit in\nfiles such as `prod.tfvars`, which a pipeline\npasses with `-var-file`. The style guide also\ncompares one repo for all configurations, a\nmonorepo, with one repo for each module\n([repository structure](https://developer.hash\nicorp.com/terraform/language/style#repository-\nstructure)).",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-90a4a9dd4a50",
      "originalText": "Repo Layouts\nThe style guide shows three ways to separate environments and parts of the system ([multiple environments](https://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/style#multiple-environments)):\n\n- One folder for each environment, such as `dev/`, `staging/` and `prod/`. Each folder has its own `backend.tf`, so each environment has its own state. All of them call the shared modules in `modules/`.\n- One folder for each part of the system, such as `networking/`, `database/` and `compute/`. Each part has its own state, so a change in one part cannot touch the objects of another part.\n- One configuration with one workspace for each environment. The Workspace node describes the limits of CLI workspaces.\n\nValues that differ by environment can sit in files such as `prod.tfvars`, which a pipeline passes with `-var-file`. The style guide also compares one repo for all configurations, a monorepo, with one repo for each module ([repository structure](https://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/style#repository-structure)).",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "repo-layouts"
      }
    },
