    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 4091365515,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "text-5b0cd6b71f86",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 1321.2,
      "y": 4800.0,
      "strokeColor": "#1E3A8A",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 394.8,
      "height": 700.0,
      "seed": 173163,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "terraform init\n#### Inputs\n\n- The `terraform` block: `required_providers`\nand the backend.\n- The `source` of each `module` block.\n- The lock file `.terraform.lock.hcl`, if it\nexists.\n- `-backend-config` values for a partial\nbackend configuration.\n\n#### Outputs\n\n- The `.terraform/` folder with the providers\nand the remote modules. In About the Examples,\ninit put the Snowflake provider in `.terraform\n/providers/registry.terraform.io/snowflakedb/s\nnowflake/2.23.0/darwin_arm64`, and the folder\nhad 52 MB.\n- The lock file. In the example, it held one\nentry, for\n`registry.terraform.io/snowflakedb/snowflake`,\nwith `version = \"2.23.0\"` and 13 checksums.\n- A connection to the backend. Init does not\nchange the state.\n\n#### Under the hood\n\nFor each provider, init uses the version in\nthe lock file. Without a lock entry, it takes\nthe newest version that matches the `version`\nconstraint and records it. Init checks each\ndownload against the checksums in the lock\nfile. `terraform init -upgrade` takes newer\nversions within the constraints ([lock file](h\nttps://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/langu\nage/files/dependency-lock)). Init is safe to\nrun many times ([init command](https://develop\ner.hashicorp.com/terraform/cli/commands/init))\n.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-5b0cd6b71f86",
      "originalText": "terraform init\n#### Inputs\n\n- The `terraform` block: `required_providers` and the backend.\n- The `source` of each `module` block.\n- The lock file `.terraform.lock.hcl`, if it exists.\n- `-backend-config` values for a partial backend configuration.\n\n#### Outputs\n\n- The `.terraform/` folder with the providers and the remote modules. In About the Examples, init put the Snowflake provider in `.terraform/providers/registry.terraform.io/snowflakedb/snowflake/2.23.0/darwin_arm64`, and the folder had 52 MB.\n- The lock file. In the example, it held one entry, for `registry.terraform.io/snowflakedb/snowflake`, with `version = \"2.23.0\"` and 13 checksums.\n- A connection to the backend. Init does not change the state.\n\n#### Under the hood\n\nFor each provider, init uses the version in the lock file. Without a lock entry, it takes the newest version that matches the `version` constraint and records it. Init checks each download against the checksums in the lock file. `terraform init -upgrade` takes newer versions within the constraints ([lock file](https://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/files/dependency-lock)). Init is safe to run many times ([init command](https://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/cli/commands/init)).",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "terraform-init"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "rectangle",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 2408382465,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "node-6d6ccb0c6521",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 1309.2,
      "y": 5060.0,
      "strokeColor": "#1E3A8A",
      "backgroundColor": "#F8FAFC",
      "width": 418.8,
      "height": 220,
      "seed": 597080,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": {
        "type": 3,
        "value": 8
      },
