    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 4077292243,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "text-6d6ccb0c6521",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 1321.2,
      "y": 5060.0,
      "strokeColor": "#1E3A8A",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 394.8,
      "height": 805.0,
      "seed": 787820,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "terraform plan\n#### Inputs\n\nThis list is all the data that goes into\nTerraform:\n\n- The configuration: every `.tf` file of the\nroot module and of the modules that it calls.\n- The variable values, from the sources that\nVariables, Locals, and Outputs lists.\n- The prior state, from the backend.\n- The real objects. The provider reads each\nobject in the state again. This step is the\nrefresh. In About the Examples, the plan\nprinted `snowflake_warehouse.agent: Refreshing\nstate... [id=\"AGENT_WH\"]`.\n- The results of the data sources, which the\nproviders read.\n- The credentials of each provider and of the\nbackend, from `provider` blocks, variables or\nenvironment variables.\n\n#### Outputs\n\n- The plan on the screen. With `-out`, also a\nsaved plan file.\n- No change to any real object. The state file\ndoes not change either: in About the Examples,\nits SHA-1 checksum was the same before and\nafter a plan.\n\n#### Under the hood\n\nThe plan command does three things ([plan comm\nand](https://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform\n/cli/commands/plan)). First, it reads the\ncurrent state of the real objects. Next, it\ncompares the configuration with that state.\nThen, it proposes the actions that remove the\ndifferences. Terraform orders the actions by a\ndependency graph, which it builds from the\nreferences between blocks. Objects that do not\ndepend on each other are handled in parallel,\n10 at a time by default. In About the\nExamples, a read-only Snowflake role was\nenough for every plan.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-6d6ccb0c6521",
      "originalText": "terraform plan\n#### Inputs\n\nThis list is all the data that goes into Terraform:\n\n- The configuration: every `.tf` file of the root module and of the modules that it calls.\n- The variable values, from the sources that Variables, Locals, and Outputs lists.\n- The prior state, from the backend.\n- The real objects. The provider reads each object in the state again. This step is the refresh. In About the Examples, the plan printed `snowflake_warehouse.agent: Refreshing state... [id=\"AGENT_WH\"]`.\n- The results of the data sources, which the providers read.\n- The credentials of each provider and of the backend, from `provider` blocks, variables or environment variables.\n\n#### Outputs\n\n- The plan on the screen. With `-out`, also a saved plan file.\n- No change to any real object. The state file does not change either: in About the Examples, its SHA-1 checksum was the same before and after a plan.\n\n#### Under the hood\n\nThe plan command does three things ([plan command](https://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/cli/commands/plan)). First, it reads the current state of the real objects. Next, it compares the configuration with that state. Then, it proposes the actions that remove the differences. Terraform orders the actions by a dependency graph, which it builds from the references between blocks. Objects that do not depend on each other are handled in parallel, 10 at a time by default. In About the Examples, a read-only Snowflake role was enough for every plan.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "terraform-plan"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "rectangle",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 9868869343,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "node-f740d3cd1c67",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 1309.2,
      "y": 5320.0,
      "strokeColor": "#1E3A8A",
      "backgroundColor": "#F8FAFC",
      "width": 418.8,
      "height": 220,
      "seed": 550372,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": {
        "type": 3,
        "value": 8
