    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 9612018693,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "text-dd9eba267178",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 730.0,
      "y": 5580.0,
      "strokeColor": "#57534E",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 390.0,
      "height": 2112.5,
      "seed": 721782,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "About the Examples\nAll outputs in this map come from runs on\n2026-11-16, with Terraform 1.15.8 on macOS\n(darwin_arm64) and the provider\n`snowflakedb/snowflake` 2.23.0. The newest\nTerraform release on that day was 1.17.2. No\n`terraform apply` ran, so nothing changed in\nSnowflake.\n\nThe first example is a folder with six files:\n\n```hcl\n# terraform.tf\nterraform {\nrequired_version = \">= 1.5\"\n\nrequired_providers {\nsnowflake = {\nsource  = \"snowflakedb/snowflake\"\nversion = \"2.23.0\"\n}\n}\n}\n\n# providers.tf\nprovider \"snowflake\" {\norganization_name = var.snowflake_organization\naccount_name      = var.snowflake_account\nuser              = var.snowflake_user\nrole              = var.snowflake_role\nauthenticator     = \"SNOWFLAKE_JWT\"\nprivate_key       = file(var.private_key_path)\n}\n\n# variables.tf\nvariable \"environment\" {\ntype        = string\ndescription = \"Short name of the environment, such\nas dev or prod.\"\n}\n\nvariable \"private_key_path\" {\ntype = string\n}\n\nvariable \"snowflake_account\" {\ntype = string\n}\n\nvariable \"snowflake_organization\" {\ntype = string\n}\n\nvariable \"snowflake_role\" {\ntype = string\n}\n\nvariable \"snowflake_user\" {\ntype = string\n}\n\n# main.tf\nlocals {\nsuffix = upper(var.environment)\n}\n\nresource \"snowflake_database\" \"raw\" {\nname    = \"RAW_${local.suffix}\"\ncomment = \"Landing zone for Kafka and Iceberg\ndata.\"\n}\n\nresource \"snowflake_warehouse\" \"transform\" {\nname           = \"TRANSFORM_${local.suffix}_WH\"\nwarehouse_size = \"XSMALL\"\nauto_suspend   = 60\n}\n\n# outputs.tf\noutput \"raw_database_name\" {\nvalue = snowflake_database.raw.name\n}\n\n# dev.tfvars\nenvironment = \"dev\"\n```\n\nThese commands ran in that folder. The role was a\nread-only role. The `TF_VAR_` variables carry the\naccount and the key, so no file holds them:\n\n```bash\nexport TF_VAR_snowflake_organization=<org>\nTF_VAR_snowflake_account=<account>\nexport TF_VAR_snowflake_user=<user>\nTF_VAR_snowflake_role=<read-only role>\nexport TF_VAR_private_key_path=<path to the .p8\nkey>\nterraform init -input=false\nterraform plan -input=false -var-file=dev.tfvars\n-out=dev.tfplan\nunzip -l dev.tfplan\n```\n\nThe second example is a copy of `terraform.tf`,\n`providers.tf` and `variables.tf` without the\nvariable `environment`, and this `main.tf`:\n\n```hcl\nresource \"snowflake_warehouse\" \"agent\" {\nname           = \"AGENT_WH\"\nwarehouse_size = \"XSMALL\"\nauto_suspend   = 300\ncomment        = \"Shared warehouse for agent\nread-only queries\"\n}\n```\n\n`AGENT_WH` is an existing X-Small warehouse with\n`AUTO_SUSPEND = 60`. These commands ran with the\nsame environment variables:\n\n```bash\nterraform init -input=false\nterraform import snowflake_warehouse.agent\n'\"AGENT_WH\"'\nshasum terraform.tfstate\nterraform plan -input=false\nshasum terraform.tfstate\n```",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 16.25,
      "containerId": "node-dd9eba267178",
      "originalText": "About the Examples\nAll outputs in this map come from runs on 2026-11-16, with Terraform 1.15.8 on macOS (darwin_arm64) and the provider `snowflakedb/snowflake` 2.23.0. The newest Terraform release on that day was 1.17.2. No `terraform apply` ran, so nothing changed in Snowflake.\n\nThe first example is a folder with six files:\n\n```hcl\n# terraform.tf\nterraform {\n  required_version = \">= 1.5\"\n\n  required_providers {\n    snowflake = {\n      source  = \"snowflakedb/snowflake\"\n      version = \"2.23.0\"\n    }\n  }\n}\n\n# providers.tf\nprovider \"snowflake\" {\n  organization_name = var.snowflake_organization\n  account_name      = var.snowflake_account\n  user              = var.snowflake_user\n  role              = var.snowflake_role\n  authenticator     = \"SNOWFLAKE_JWT\"\n  private_key       = file(var.private_key_path)\n}\n\n# variables.tf\nvariable \"environment\" {\n  type        = string\n  description = \"Short name of the environment, such as dev or prod.\"\n}\n\nvariable \"private_key_path\" {\n  type = string\n}\n\nvariable \"snowflake_account\" {\n  type = string\n}\n\nvariable \"snowflake_organization\" {\n  type = string\n}\n\nvariable \"snowflake_role\" {\n  type = string\n}\n\nvariable \"snowflake_user\" {\n  type = string\n}\n\n# main.tf\nlocals {\n  suffix = upper(var.environment)\n}\n\nresource \"snowflake_database\" \"raw\" {\n  name    = \"RAW_${local.suffix}\"\n  comment = \"Landing zone for Kafka and Iceberg data.\"\n}\n\nresource \"snowflake_warehouse\" \"transform\" {\n  name           = \"TRANSFORM_${local.suffix}_WH\"\n  warehouse_size = \"XSMALL\"\n  auto_suspend   = 60\n}\n\n# outputs.tf\noutput \"raw_database_name\" {\n  value = snowflake_database.raw.name\n}\n\n# dev.tfvars\nenvironment = \"dev\"\n```\n\nThese commands ran in that folder. The role was a read-only role. The `TF_VAR_` variables carry the account and the key, so no file holds them:\n\n```bash\nexport TF_VAR_snowflake_organization=<org> TF_VAR_snowflake_account=<account>\nexport TF_VAR_snowflake_user=<user> TF_VAR_snowflake_role=<read-only role>\nexport TF_VAR_private_key_path=<path to the .p8 key>\nterraform init -input=false\nterraform plan -input=false -var-file=dev.tfvars -out=dev.tfplan\nunzip -l dev.tfplan\n```\n\nThe second example is a copy of `terraform.tf`, `providers.tf` and `variables.tf` without the variable `environment`, and this `main.tf`:\n\n```hcl\nresource \"snowflake_warehouse\" \"agent\" {\n  name           = \"AGENT_WH\"\n  warehouse_size = \"XSMALL\"\n  auto_suspend   = 300\n  comment        = \"Shared warehouse for agent read-only queries\"\n}\n```\n\n`AGENT_WH` is an existing X-Small warehouse with `AUTO_SUSPEND = 60`. These commands ran with the same environment variables:\n\n```bash\nterraform init -input=false\nterraform import snowflake_warehouse.agent '\"AGENT_WH\"'\nshasum terraform.tfstate\nterraform plan -input=false\nshasum terraform.tfstate\n```",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "about-the-examples"
      }
    },
